{"Id":"T:PressToShape.Benchmarks.PathOperationBenchmarks","Name":"PathOperationBenchmarks","QualifiedName":"PressToShape.Benchmarks.PathOperationBenchmarks","SymbolType":"Class","Accessibility":"public","Modifiers":[],"ContainingId":"N:PressToShape.Benchmarks","Namespace":"PressToShape.Benchmarks","Project":"PressToShape.Benchmarks","File":"tests/PressToShape.Benchmarks/PathOperationBenchmarks.cs","StartLine":15,"EndLine":66,"Parameters":[],"Attributes":[{"Name":"MemoryDiagnoser","Arguments":[]}],"Interfaces":[],"IsGenerated":false,"Doc":{"HasDocumentation":true,"Summary":"How long a boolean operation takes for two overlapping outlines with the same number of curved nodes each. The 200 node case is the budget of the requirements (under 200 ms); the larger sizes show where the work should leave the UI thread (PressToShape.Core.PathOperations.BooleanEngine.BackgroundNodeLimit). Total nodes are twice the parameter.","Params":{},"Exceptions":[]}},
